# GMS's readout ends "Final damage increases by 15% with each enemy pierced,
# and damage is doubled". Neither is here: an arrow that gains as it travels
# needs an order to travel along, and every enemy in reach takes the same
# damage in this game. Dropped rather than averaged -- folding the escalation
# in would put the Crossbowman a third ahead of the Hunter on a full screen
# and level with them on one mob, which is a worse lie than leaving it out.
name: "Piercing Arrow"
skill_order: 1
description:
  "One bolt, driven hard enough to pass clean through the line. Fires an "
  "arrow through the enemies in front of you."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ATTACK
job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_CROSSBOWMAN
max_level: 20
base_delay_ms: 780
max_enemies: 6
lines: 4
base { skill_pct: 0.92 }
per_level { skill_pct: 0.02 }
